          "text": "Base directory for this skill: /Users/hk00691ml/.claude/skills/remove-ai-flavor\n\n# Remove AI Flavor\n\n## Overview\n\nAI 味 = a predictable layer of **stylistic tells** sitting on top of the content. The substance is usually fine; the packaging screams \"an LLM wrote this.\" This skill strips the tells and keeps every fact, number, decision, caveat, and link intact.\n\n**The iron rule: change style, never meaning.** If a rewrite drops, adds, or shifts information, it failed — no matter how much better it reads. You are de-slopping prose, not editing content.\n\n## The One Constraint You Cannot Break\n\nPreserve, exactly: every fact, number, date, named decision, caveat/risk, TODO, link, filename, code block, table cell, and technical term. Do not invent. Do not summarize content away. Do not soften or strengthen a claim.\n\nStructure that carries information (headings, tables, status labels) **stays** — only *decorative* structure goes. A ✅/⚠️ that means \"已定 / 待办\" is information: convert it to the plain word (`已定：` / `待办：`), don't just delete the status.\n\n## The Tells (scan for these, rewrite each)\n\n| AI tell | Why it reads as AI | Human rewrite |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Emoji as markers** (✅⚠️🚩🌱🔥📝) sprinkled on headings/bullets | Decorative status theater | Delete decorative ones; convert semantic ones to plain words (`已定：`, `风险：`) |\n| **Bold-everything** — `**关键词**` in nearly every sentence | Emphasis inflation → nothing stands out | Keep bold for genuinely load-bearing terms only (roughly ≤1 per paragraph); unbold the rest |\n| **Em-dash / 破折号 drama** — `——` for a \"pause then reveal\" | Manufactured suspense | Use a period or comma; restructure into a plain sentence |\n| **\"不是 X，而是 Y\" / \"not just X, but Y\"** antithesis | Rhetorical template | State it plainly: \"Y。（X 做不到 Z）\" |\n| **Rule-of-three / 排比** — `去噪、去重、结构化`, `可读、可编辑、可 git` | Rhythm for its own sake | Keep when genuinely enumerating distinct things; cut the ones that only exist for cadence |\n| **Bilingual slogan echoes** — `先蒸馏，再检索 / Distill, then retrieve` | Copywriter tic | Keep one version where it's actually used; drop the echo |\n| **Meta / self-narration** — \"这份文档是什么\", \"TL;DR\", \"一句话 / 一句更短的\", \"本节说明\" | Talks about the doc instead of saying the thing | Cut the framing; keep the actual content it introduces |\n| **Hype words** — 极简 / 硬功夫 / 最有说服力 / 引爆 / 丝滑 / seamless / game-changer | Marketing gloss | Cut, or replace with the concrete fact (\"一行命令启动\") |\n| **Formulaic transitions** — 值得注意的是 / 综上所述 / 首先…其次…最后 / It's worth noting / In conclusion | Essay-bot scaffolding | Delete; let sentences connect directly |\n| **Self-declared honesty/transparency** — 坦白说 / 说实话 / 需要坦诚的是 / Honest trade-offs / I'm upfront about / To be transparent | LLMs announce their own candor; humans just say the thing | Drop the meta-label, state it directly (`Trade-offs:` / `Fair warning:`) |\n| **Appreciation / 附和 opener** — \"这是一个很好的直觉\" / \"好方向\" / \"好问题\" / \"有道理\" / \"You're absolutely right\" / \"Great point\" before the real content | AI reflexively validates before answering | Cut the praise; lead straight with the substance or your actual judgment |\n| **English LLM vocabulary tells** — delve / leverage / robust / seamless / tapestry / underscore / pivotal / realm / landscape / testament / \"a wide range of\" / \"it's worth noting\" / \"let's dive in\" | Statistical fingerprints of LLM prose | Swap for the plain word (use → not leverage, show → not underscore, strong → not robust); delete filler openers |\n| **Grand opening** — \"在当今快速发展的…时代\" / \"众所周知\" / \"In today's fast-paced world\" / \"In the ever-evolving landscape of\" | Essay windup before saying anything | Delete; open on the actual first fact |\n| **Summary recap ending** — a closing paragraph that restates what was just said (\"综上，我们探讨了…\" / \"In summary, we've covered…\") | Book-report reflex | Delete, or end on the last real point / next action |\n| **Rhetorical-question transition** — \"那么这意味着什么？\" / \"So what does this mean?\" / \"问题来了：\" as a segue | Manufactured pacing | Just make the next statement |\n| **中文职场黑话堆叠** — 赋能 / 抓手 / 闭环 / 对齐 / 生态位 / 打法 / 组合拳 used as filler | Corporate-AI register | Say the concrete action (\"赋能业务\" → \"帮业务做 X\"); keep a term only if it's the precise word |\n| **Templated callouts** — repeated `> **决策**：` / `> **给你的动作**：` blocks | Uniform, machine-stamped | Keep the info, drop the repeated label wrapper, or use a normal sentence/heading |\n| **Hedge+booster stack** — 大概率 / 往往 / 极其 / 基本上 | LLM caution reflex | Say it directly or give the actual condition |\n| **Uniform bullet shape** — every bullet same length/structure | Too regular to be human | Vary length; merge trivial bullets into prose; let some points be one word, others a sentence |\n| **Glyphs humans rarely hand-type** — circled/fancy numerals ①②③ / ➊ / ⓵ as bullets, section sign `§4.6` for cross-refs, \"其一…其二…\" as list markers | Humans reach for plain keys; these glyphs are a tell even when the list/reference itself is fine | Plain `1. 2. 3.` list or a label instead of circled numerals; write \"见 4.6 节\" / \"第 4.6 节\" instead of `§4.6` |\n\n**Positive target (what human writing looks like):** varied sentence length, the point stated first, plain punctuation, facts left to stand on their own without bolding, no throat-clearing before content, occasional imperfection over relentless polish.\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Read the whole doc first.** Note what information each section actually carries — you'll protect it.\n2. **Rewrite section by section**, applying the table. For each edit ask: did any fact/decision/link move? If yes, undo.\n3. **Preserve the scaffold that means something** — tables, headings, code, status labels (converted to words).\n4. **Don't over-correct.** The goal is \"a sharp human wrote this,\" not \"terse robot.\" Keep it readable and complete; don't strip nuance, don't flatten every list into one line.\n5. **Self-check before delivering** (below).\n\n## Before / After (real pattern)\n\n**Before (AI-flavored):**\n> ✅ **决策（2026-07）**：**保持 `kaas` 不变**——英文名不用 \"distillation\"（避撞 ML 术语），「蒸馏」作**中文叙事主线**、\"distill\" 作**英文动词 tagline**。\n\n**After (de-slopped, same meaning):**\n> 决策（2026-07）：仓库名保持 `kaas`。英文名不用 \"distillation\"，避免和 ML 术语撞车；「蒸馏」用作中文叙事主线，\"distill\" 作英文 tagline 的动词。\n\nWhat changed: dropped ✅, unbolded decorative bold, replaced `——` drama with a plain sentence break. What stayed: the date, the decision, the reason, both terms, their roles.\n\n## Self-Check (before you deliver)\n\n- [ ] Every number, date, decision, caveat, link, filename, code block, table cell still present and unchanged?\n- [ ] No claim softened, strengthened, added, or invented?\n- [ ] Decorative emoji/bold gone; semantic status converted to words, not deleted?\n- [ ] Does it read like a knowledgeable person wrote it in one sitting — varied rhythm, no template feel?\n- [ ] Did I avoid over-correcting into terse/robotic? Nuance intact?\n\nIf rewriting a file in place: show the user a summary of what stylistic changes you made and confirm no content moved. For a long doc, a quick `diff` review of a few sections beats a wall of text.\n\n## Verify with a Blind Judge\n\nSelf-review misses your own tells. To measure whether the de-slopping actually worked, dispatch a **fresh subagent** (no context on who wrote it or that it was de-slopped) and ask it to score AI-flavor 0–100 and cite specific tells.\n\n- **Keep it blind.** New agent, new context each run. Don't tell it the doc was rewritten — that biases it toward \"improved.\"\n- **Score deliverable copy separately from framing.** Marketing/technical copy meant to ship (HN/Reddit posts, taglines) follows genre conventions and scores differently from the doc's own narration; judge them apart so a conventional-but-fine post doesn't drag the verdict.\n- **Trust the verdict, not the number.** Run-to-run variance is ±6 or more; a 22 vs 28 swing between runs is noise. What's stable is the conclusion (\"would/wouldn't read as AI\") and the *specific* tells cited. Stop when the verdict is stable — chasing the number down is fighting judge variance.\n- **A stronger judge is worth one pass.** After stabilizing with a cheap model, one run from a more capable model catches subtler tells (self-declared honesty, appreciation openers) the cheaper one waves through.\n- **Fold new tells back here.** Every distinct tell a judge finds that isn't in the table above → add a row. That's how this skill grew.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n- **Deleting status markers instead of converting them** → loses \"已定/待办\" information. Convert.\n- **\"Improving\" content while de-slopping** → out of scope. Style only; flag content issues separately, don't fix silently.\n- **Over-flattening** → turning a useful three-item list into one comma sentence when the items are genuinely distinct. Rhythm-triads go; real enumerations stay.\n- **Trading one tell for another** → replacing 综上所述 with \"Bottom line:\" is still a tell. Just start the sentence.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: py/README.md — 我刚把这份中文 README 整篇译成英文（技术参考型文档：安装、daemon 协议、命令表、CLI、环境变量表）。要求：保持原意与信息零丢失，只去掉 AI 腔。",
